  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive). Transitive pair: {散|ち}らかす (to make messy).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates resulting state. {散|ち}らかっている = 'is messy' (state).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {部屋|へや}が{散|ち}らかる (room becomes messy)\n- Xが{散|ち}らかっている (X is scattered/messy)\n- {散|ち}らかった{部屋|へや} (a messy room)\n\nTRANSITIVE PAIR:\n- {散|ち}らかる (intransitive) - to be messy\n- {散|ち}らかす (transitive) - to make messy\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {乱|みだ}れる - to be in disorder (more general)\n- {散|ち}る - to scatter, fall (like petals)",
